# Playwright Enhance

> 🚀 Performance-enhanced Playwright wrapper designed for AI agents like OpenClaw

[![CI](https://github.com/playwright-enhance/playwright-enhance/workflows/CI/badge.svg)](https://github.com/playwright-enhance/playwright-enhance/actions)
[![PyPI version](https://badge.fury.io/py/playwright-enhance.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/playwright-enhance/)
[![Python 3.8+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.8+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

## Overview

Playwright Enhance is a performance-optimized wrapper for Playwright that significantly speeds up browser automation for AI agents. It reduces waiting time by 50%+ and element location time by 60%+ through intelligent optimization strategies.

### Key Features

- 🎯 **Smart Waiting**: Adaptive timeouts (1-10s) instead of fixed 30s waits
- 🔍 **Multi-Locator**: Semantic + Visual + DOM element location strategies  
- ⚡ **Concurrent Operations**: Intelligent batching and parallel execution
- 💾 **Smart Caching**: Multi-level cache system with automatic invalidation
- 🤖 **AI-Friendly API**: Natural language operations (`smart_click`, `batch_execute`)
- 📊 **Performance Monitoring**: Real-time metrics and bottleneck identification
- 🛠️ **CLI Tool**: Command-line interface for quick automation

### Performance Gains

- **3-5x faster** overall execution compared to native Playwright
- **60-70% → 30%** reduction in time spent waiting
- **15-20% → 5-8%** reduction in element location time

## Installation

```bash
pip install playwright-enhance
playwright install chromium  # Install browser binaries
```

## Quick Start

```python
from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright
from playwright_enhance import enhance

with sync_playwright() as p:
    browser = p.chromium.launch()
    page = enhance(browser.new_page())  # ✨ Enhanced page
    
    # Use native Playwright API (fully compatible)
    page.goto("https://example.com")
    page.click("#button")
    
    # Or use AI-friendly semantic operations
    page.smart_click("login button")
    page.smart_fill("username field", "admin")
    
    # Batch operations for maximum speed
    page.batch_execute([
        ("fill", "username", "admin"),
        ("fill", "password", "secret"),
        ("click", "submit button")
    ])
```

## CLI Usage

```bash
# Execute natural language commands
playwright-enhance-cli exec "open google and search for playwright"

# Run YAML scripts
playwright-enhance-cli run automation.yaml

# Performance benchmarking
playwright-enhance-cli benchmark https://example.com

# Interactive debugger
playwright-enhance-cli inspect https://example.com
```

